From 29ec5302d7f92c69c8d2a9fc2acaf907e86d800e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anurodh Pokharel <anurodhp@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 11:53:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] do_command.c: drop IOKit/CoreFoundation/vproc/launchd
 bootstrap glue

Real Apple source here does two things this project's from-source
XNU-on-Raspberry-Pi-3 port has no infrastructure for at all:

1. Skips a job if entry->flags has NOT_BATTERY set and the board is
   running on battery and not charging (IOPMCopyBatteryInfo() +
   CoreFoundation dictionary/array/number access). This board has no
   battery - real scope decision, always run these jobs, not a gap.

2. Re-points this process's Mach bootstrap port at the target user's
   per-user launchd bootstrap namespace before exec'ing the job
   (bootstrap_look_up_per_user() + task_set_bootstrap_port(), "similar
   to but simpler than pam_launchd") and pings vproc to reset exception
   ports for it. This project has no launchd and no per-user bootstrap
   namespaces - real scope decision, not a gap. The real uid/gid/HOME
   privilege-drop logic just above this block (getpwnam/getgrnam/
   env_set) is untouched.

Both blocks needed headers (IOKit/*, CoreFoundation/*, vproc.h,
vproc_priv.h, bootstrap_priv.h) that don't exist anywhere in this
project's Libc/XNU pull, so this isn't optional - the file would not
compile otherwise. Everything else in do_command.c (fork/exec, pipe
plumbing, privilege drop, environment setup, logging) is untouched real
Apple source.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015TwUDDSuuyGNDakVeLuokc
